            "notes": "identifier/ontology_id CHEBI:43968 ('meropenem') -> CHEBI:6770 ('meropenem trihydrate'). The record's own cas_rn 119478-56-7 is registered by ChEBI against CHEBI:6770, which is the trihydrate of the term the record previously carried. Curation decision on #320: where the CAS names a more specific FORM than the label, the CAS governs — the recipe is taken to mean the substance actually weighed out. These surfaced as 'unrelated' in the ancestry triage only because ChEBI does not model salt-of / hydrate-of / racemate-of as subsumption, the same gap #342 recorded for hydrates."
